# tally 2.3.1 N256.7, P44 (L §2.4 Values, a check's sides in their types): a declared `%` side prints in its
# type beside a hole too (c2: `p = 10 %`), and the difference of two `%` sides prints with `%` (c1:
# `difference -20 %`). Before: `p = 0.1` beside the hole, `difference -0.2`.
=== chkpct1.tally
model b3
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "probe"
input p: num %
input q: num %
input ph: num %

ask c1: check p == q
ask c2: check p == ph

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  p = 10 % "s"
  q = 30 % "s"
  ph = ?"which?" "s"
=== expect
c1: differs: p = 10 %, q = 30 %, difference -20 %
  cut 2026-06-30
c2: p = 10 %, ph = ?"which?" (ph)
  cut 2026-06-30
